<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Okinawa Island</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Okinawa Island is the largest island of the Ryukyu chain, between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyushu">Kyushu</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taiwan">Taiwan</a>, and the site of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naha">Naha</a>, capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/okinawa-prefecture">Okinawa Prefecture</a>. In the 14th century it was divided among the three kingdoms of Hokuzan, Chuzan and Nanzan, united in 1429 as the Ryukyu Kingdom with its court at Shuri. Annexed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> in 1879, it was the scene of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-okinawa">Battle of Okinawa</a> in 1945 and remained under American administration until 1972.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/okinawa-island.jpg" alt="Okinawa Island" width="320" height="379" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Image Science and Analysis Laboratory, NASA - Johnson Space Center. &quot;The Gateway to Astronaut Photography of Earth.&quot; · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Okinawa_Island-ISS042.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
